Then I just start opencode, type something, press enter.

thanks for reporting. this is a type generation issue in the default sdk export, not a server/runtime issue. structured output is supported by the api, and the v2 sdk types already include `format`.
for now, you can use the v2 import:
```ts
import { createOpencodeClient } from "@opencode-ai/sdk/v2"
note that the v2 sdk uses the newer flat parameter shape, so the call would look like:
await opencodeClient.session.prompt({
  sessionID: session.id,
  parts: [
    { type: "text", text: "Research Anthropic and provide company info" },
  ],
  format: {
    type: "json_schema",
    schema: {
      type: "object",
      properties: {
        company: { type: "string" },
        founded: { type: "number" },
      },
      required: ["company", "founded"],
    },
  },
})

I am on Windows. No, auto-compaction is never triggered i always have to manually trigger it (when I realize that the model doesn't answer anymore).

Our LiteLLM sends back custom error messages (non provider-typical) so maybe OpenCode doesn't detect the context full therefore. What I'd appreciate here is if OpenCode allowed you to SEE any upstream error messages. But it doesn't surface them in the chat.

